    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "What Orthodontists Recommend"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Most orthodontists suggest clear aligners or retainers for mild to moderate teeth straightening. For complex bite correction or poor jaw development, traditional braces are still the safest route."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It’s about balance, comfort, cost, and the kind of smile you want. Clear systems work well for adults who want freedom and for teens who prefer less visible options."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A quick consultation can help you find what suits your mouth best. Some people need hybrid plans, aligners for the upper teeth and braces for the lower ones."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Final Thoughts"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "So, can you really straighten teeth without braces? Yes, in most cases, you can. But it’s not a one-size-fits-all story. The right method depends on your alignment, jaw, and oral health."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If you’re unsure where to start, visit Dr Dante Gonzales Orthodontics. The team will check your case, suggest the best and most efficient options, and guide you toward your beautiful smile, with or without braces."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Straightening teeth without braces takes discipline and trust in the process. But once you see your new smile, you’ll know it was worth every small effort."
    },
