    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1. Can you straighten your teeth without braces? Yes, you can. Treatments like clear aligners, retainers, or cosmetic reshaping can help straighten teeth without braces depending on your case. 2. How long does teeth straightening without braces take? It usually takes 4 to 24 months. The time depends on how crooked teeth are and how consistently you wear your aligners. 3. Are clear aligners better than metal braces? For mild to moderate alignment, yes. They’re invisible, removable, and comfortable. But metal braces are usually better for severe misalignments and malocclusions. 4. Can adults straighten their teeth? Absolutely. Orthodontic treatment works for adults too. Just like in children, bone in adults can reshape with controlled force, leading to a lasting, straight smile. 5. Is teeth straightening only about looks? No. Proper alignment prevents tooth decay, tooth loss, improves oral health, and helps maintain healthier gums. Straight teeth make cleaning and chewing much easier."
    }
